The official Amiga binaries are now available for anonymous ftp from
linc.cis.upenn.edu (130.91.6.8) in pub/NH3.1/binaries/amiga.  Please
restrict transfers to non-business hours (USA east coast time).

The distribution consists of two .lzh files and a file called readmefirst.
The sizes of the two .lzh files are:
	415045 NH31P0-1.lzh
	377367 NH31P0-2.lzh

NetHack is copyrighted but freely redistributable - please see the file
license in the distribution for details.

		Amiga NetHack 3.1 -- System Requirements
Amiga NetHack requires:
  - Amiga 500, 1000, 2000, 3000, 4000 with WorkBench 1.3 or greater.
  - At least two meg of RAM.
  - A hard disk with three or more meg free, or two floppy drives (this will
    not be easy, but it should work).


                Amiga NetHack 3.1 -- Transferring
Be sure to retrieve the two .lzh files in BINARY mode or they will
not work.  To set binary mode in most versions of ftp type:
  set binary

  
                Amiga NetHack 3.1 -- Unpacking

The Amiga NetHack binary distribution comes in two .lzh files:  If you
are unpacking to floppy unpack each archive on a different disk; if you
are unpacking to a harddisk unpack them both to the same directory.
Installation instructions are in the ReadMe file in the top level
directory of the second file.

For problems with the archives or with the game please contact
keni@oasys.dt.navy.mil or use the central address
nethack-bugs@linc.cis.upenn.edu.  Please mention that you are using
the official Amiga binaries.

